1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,250
Why does the Moon change shape?

2
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:06,220
Does the Moon change shape
because of Earth's shadow?

3
00:00:06,270 --> 00:00:09,990
Nope! When the shadow covers it,
that's a rare "lunar eclipse"

4
00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:12,760
Seen from above,
the half of the Moon facing the Sun is always lit

5
00:00:12,810 --> 00:00:15,130
As the Moon goes around Earth,
how much of the lit side we see changes

6
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:18,530
Crescent → half moon

7
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:20,330
On the far side from the Sun: full moon!

8
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:22,530
Half moon again

9
00:00:22,580 --> 00:00:24,730
Thin crescent → gone → a new crescent again

10
00:00:24,780 --> 00:00:28,500
One trip around takes about a month!

11
00:00:28,550 --> 00:00:33,470
Face a lamp, hold up a ball,
and slowly turn in place

12
00:00:33,520 --> 00:00:36,840
The lit part of the ball
changes just like the Moon

13
00:00:36,890 --> 00:00:39,090
What changes is the angle we see it from

14
00:00:39,140 --> 00:00:41,590
NEXT: What if you cut a magnet in half?
